{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Lens flare fixture (spec 11.21). One small bright emissive quad up and to",
    "the LEFT on a black backdrop, which is the only configuration a ghost",
    "chain is measurable in: ghosts are the source mirrored through frame",
    "centre, so they owe the lower-right, and a scene with large bright areas",
    "would put a source in every pixel and read as a wash instead.",
    "",
    "The zero-intensity light is not lighting -- it is how a scene declines the",
    "three-point rig the render app adds when a scene declares none (the",
    "oit_cards idiom). That rig lifts the backdrop off black and dilutes the",
    "measurement: the opposite-half rise is +3.5% with it and +276% without.",
    "",
    "A second, DIM quad sits in the far corner for the chromatic-aberration",
    "assertion, which needs a high-contrast edge at large radius. At emissive",
    "0.6 it is below the bloom threshold, so it never enters the pyramid and",
    "casts no ghosts -- it cannot disturb the flare measurement.",
    "",
    "Bloom stays ON because the flare reads its pyramid. Exposure is pinned so",
    "two runs compare."
  ],
  "models": [ { "path": "flare_fixture.gltf" } ],
  "lights": [
    {
      "name": "flare_no_rig",
      "type": "directional",
      "direction": [0.0, -1.0, 0.0],
      "intensity": 0.0
    }
  ],
  "camera": { "eye": [0.0, 0.0, 5.0], "target": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "fov": 50 },
  "post": {
    "tonemap": "neutral",
    "exposure": 1.0,
    "auto_exposure": false,
    "bloom": { "enabled": true }
  }
}
